local _, ns = ...
local E = ns.DB.entries
E["npc:arugal"] = {t="npc",n="Arugal",z="shadowfang",s="Archmage Arugal is a former wizard of Dalaran and Gilneas who unleashed the feral worgen upon Lordaeron. Overcome by madness and grief, he now rules from the heights of Shadowfang Keep, treating the savage beasts as his beloved children while menacing all of Silverpine Forest.",h="Archmage Arugal is a former wizard of Dalaran and Gilneas who unleashed the feral worgen upon Lordaeron.",sec={{t="A Desperate Summons",b="Before the fall of Lordaeron, Arugal was a member of the Kirin Tor, though some peers like Dalar Dawnweaver dismissed him as a charlatan whose weak spellcraft relied heavily on enchanted trinkets. When the Scourge swept across the north during the Third War, Arugal sought a weapon powerful enough to stem the tide. Drawing upon the esoteric research of the late Dalaran mage Ur, Arugal pierced the veil between realms and summoned the worgen into the mortal world. The ravenous beasts tore through the undead legions as intended, but their feral ferocity could not be contained, and their savage hunger swiftly turned against innocent mortals.",sp=0},{t="Fall into Madness",b="The summoned horrors slaughtered the Gilnean soldiers stationed outside the Greymane Wall and spread their dreadful affliction across northern Silverpine. Rather than flee from his monstrous creation, Arugal's mind fractured under the weight of guilt. He adopted the beasts as his own offspring and led them against the ancestral seat of Baron Silverlaine. The keep fell swiftly to claws and fangs, its lord and retainers slain in the massacre. Renaming the fortress Shadowfang Keep, Arugal entrenched himself within its ramparts, surrounded by ghostly victims and loyal hound-packs.",sp=0},{t="The Scourge of Silverpine",b="From his high perch in Shadowfang Keep, Arugal extends his twisted dominion over the surrounding countryside. His dark sorcery blankets Pyrewood Village, where townsfolk live under a nocturnal curse, and infests the Deep Elem Mine with ravenous Moonrage beasts. He works intricate enchantments allowing select favored servants to retain human intellect while yielding entirely to his will. Both the Kirin Tor and the Forsaken now view him as an intolerable threat; Sylvanas Windrunner's Deathstalkers and apothecaries actively plot the mad archmage's execution to secure the borders of their fledgling kingdom.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Arugal?",a="Arugal is a former human archmage of the Kirin Tor and Gilneas. Driven mad during the Third War, he summoned the monstrous worgen to battle the Scourge. Overwhelmed by his actions, he retreated into Shadowfang Keep, where he now leads packs of worgen as their self-proclaimed father.",al={"who is arugal","arugal backstory","shadowfang boss lore"}},{q="Why did Arugal summon the worgen?",a="During the Third War, the Scourge threatened to overrun northern Lordaeron and Gilneas. Desperate for a weapon to halt the undead, Arugal utilized the extraplanar research of the Dalaran mage Ur. He believed the savage beasts could destroy the Scourge, but he lost control of the creatures once summoned.",al={"why worgen","why summon beasts","arugal worgen motive"}},{q="Where does Arugal reside right now?",a="Arugal makes his lair at the pinnacle of Shadowfang Keep, an ancient fortress situated on the sea cliffs above Pyrewood Village in southern Silverpine Forest. He is guarded by his monstrous wolf pet, Fenrus, alongside swarms of loyal worgen and restless spirits.",al={"where is arugal","arugal location","find arugal"}},{q="What happened to Baron Silverlaine?",a="Baron Silverlaine was the noble lord who originally ruled the fortress and the village of Pyrewood. When Arugal's worgen besieged the castle, Silverlaine and his court were brutally slaughtered. Their vengeful, tortured ghosts now haunt the blood-stained halls of the keep.",al={"baron silverlaine fate","who owned shadowfang","keep history"}},{q="Why do the Forsaken want Arugal dead?",a="Arugal's packs terrorize Silverpine Forest, attacking Forsaken scouts, ambushing patrols, and even infecting loyal servants of the Royal Apothecary Society. Sylvanas Windrunner considers the mad archmage a direct threat to the security and expansion of the Undercity's borders.",al={"forsaken vs arugal","arugal must die quest","why kill arugal"}},{q="What is the curse on Pyrewood Village?",a="Arugal cast wretched enchantments across the region, subjecting the human inhabitants of Pyrewood Village to the worgen curse. By daylight, the villagers appear as normal human subjects, but come nightfall, they transform into vicious beasts bound to defend Arugal's territory.",al={"pyrewood curse","why are pyrewood villagers wolves","pyrewood arugal"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Arugal's worgen infest the road south of the Sepulcher, and Lady Sylvanas has ordered his execution to secure Silverpine Forest for the Forsaken.",["race:Undead"]="Arugal's beasts have killed several Deathstalkers and apothecaries; putting an end to his madness is a vital task for the Royal Apothecary Society.",["class:Mage"]="Arugal represents the catastrophic danger of reckless conjuration, turning the deep research of the Kirin Tor into an uncontrollable nightmare."},kw={"arugal","kirin tor","pyrewood","shadowfang","silverlaine","silverpine","ur","worgen"},rel={"zone:shadowfang","zone:silverpine","topic:worgen","quest:1014","quest:99","subzone:pyrewood-village","npc:baron-silverlaine","npc:dalar-dawnweaver"},src={"Arugal"}}
E["npc:baron-silverlaine"] = {t="npc",n="Baron Silverlaine",z="shadowfang",s="Baron Silverlaine was the rightful human lord of the fortress once known as Keep Silverlaine, perched high above Pyrewood Village. When Archmage Arugal unleashed the savage worgen upon the region, the baron and his household were mercilessly slaughtered. Now, his tormented spirit lingers in the ruined dining hall, bound in undeath to defend the very lair that became his tomb.",h="Baron Silverlaine was the rightful human lord of the fortress once known as Keep Silverlaine, perched high...",sec={{t="The Fall of Keep Silverlaine",b="Before the shadow of the wolf-beasts blanketed the southern hills of Silverpine, Baron Silverlaine ruled over a proud noble estate. His fortress provided safety and oversight to the surrounding Gilnean lands. That peace shattered when Archmage Arugal, seeking a weapon against the rampaging Scourge, unleashed summoned worgen into the region. The feral monstrosities could not be controlled; they stormed the stronghold, overran its guards, and butchered the baron along with his entire family.",sp=0},{t="A Tormented Specter",b="Death brought no release to Baron Silverlaine. Bound to the keep's ancient Great Hall, his restless ghost now wanders the trashed dining tables where he once feasted. In a cruel twist of dark magic, the cursed lord lashes out at any intruders who enter his ruined home, strangely compelled to summon the spectral forms of the very beasts that tore his flesh apart in life.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Baron Silverlaine?",a="He was the noble Gilnean human master of the fortress originally named Keep Silverlaine, situated above Pyrewood Village. He was slain alongside his family when worgen overran the fortress.",al={"baron silverlaine lore","who is silverlaine","who ruled shadowfang"}},{q="Why is he haunting Shadowfang Keep?",a="Silverlaine was slaughtered in his own home during the worgen onslaught unleashed by Archmage Arugal. Cursed in death, his ghost remains tethered to the dining hall of his ruined keep, unable to move on.",al={"why is silverlaine a ghost","is silverlaine dead","silverlaine spirit"}},{q="Why does he summon worgen spirits if they killed him?",a="The dark curse binding him within Shadowfang Keep twists his tragic fate into a perpetual nightmare. In his spectral madness, the baron's anguish manifests the phantoms of the very wolf-beasts that butchered his household.",al={"why does silverlaine use worgen","silverlaine worgen ghosts","silverlaine adds"}},{q="Where in the keep can he be found?",a="Baron Silverlaine haunts the Great Hall, which served as the keep's lavish dining room before it was wrecked during the fall of his estate.",al={"where is silverlaine","baron silverlaine location","silverlaine dining hall"}},{q="What was Shadowfang Keep called before the worgen attack?",a="It was originally called Keep Silverlaine, named after the baron's noble family who held dominion over it before Arugal took control.",al={"shadowfang original name","keep silverlaine lore","old name of shadowfang"}},{q="Did anyone in Silverlaine's family survive?",a="No. Historical accounts confirm that Baron Silverlaine and his entire family were slaughtered inside the keep when the feral worgen invaded.",al={"silverlaine family","did silverlaines family live","silverlaine heirs"}}},ang={["race:Human"]="Silverlaine stands as a bitter testament to the downfall of human noble authority on the borders of Gilneas, his family wiped out by the magical hubris of a Dalaran-trained wizard.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken pushing across Silverpine, Silverlaine's specter is merely another remnant of old Gilnean aristocracy that must be cleared to break Arugal's grip on the keep.",["class:Mage"]="Silverlaine's fate serves as a grim warning of magical recklessness; the summoner's art, when mishandled as Archmage Arugal did, destroys innocent lives and leaves indelible scars."},kw={"arugal","baron","ghost","great hall","keep","pyrewood","shadowfang","silverlaine","worgen"},rel={"zone:shadowfang","npc:arugal","topic:worgen","topic:scourge","topic:alliance","topic:horde"},src={"Baron Silverlaine"}}
E["npc:commander-springvale"] = {t="npc",n="Commander Springvale",z="shadowfang",s="Commander Springvale was once a devoted paladin and the head of Baron Silverlaine's armed guard at Shadowfang Keep. Slain alongside his men during the feral worgen slaughter orchestrated by Archmage Arugal, his vengeful spirit remains behind to haunt the castle halls. Even in death, his ghost fiercely guards the keep and seeks vengeance for his fallen master.",h="Commander Springvale was once a devoted paladin and the head of Baron Silverlaine's armed guard at Shadowfang...",sec={{t="The Fallen Commander",b="Before the ruin of Shadowfang Keep, Commander Springvale stood as an honorable paladin dedicated to the Holy Light and a sworn defender of Baron Silverlaine. Leading the garrison in Silverpine Forest, he oversaw the keep's security during the fraught days following the fall of Lordaeron to the Scourge.",sp=0},{t="Arugal's Folly",b="When Archmage Arugal summoned the extraplanar worgen to repel the undead Scourge encroaching upon Gilnean soil, the wild beasts quickly slipped from the mage's control. The ravenous pack descended upon the fortress, slaughtering Baron Silverlaine and his entire guard. Springvale perished in the halls he had sworn to protect, his service violently cut short.",sp=0},{t="An Unholy Vigil",b="Death offered no release to Springvale's bound soul. Twisted by trauma and necromantic energy, his ghost lingers within the keep's stone chambers. Though he carried the teachings of the Light in life, his phantom now strikes out with unholy power, blindly executing an eternal duty to avenge the slain Baron against any trespasser who sets foot inside the keep.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Commander Springvale in life?",a="Commander Springvale was a paladin of the Holy Light who served as the commander of Baron Silverlaine's armed forces. He was tasked with the defense of Shadowfang Keep and remained fiercely loyal to the Baron until his death.",al={"springvale backstory","who is commander springvale","is springvale a paladin"}},{q="How did Commander Springvale die?",a="He was killed when Archmage Arugal summoned feral worgen to fight the Scourge. The untamed beasts turned upon the inhabitants of Shadowfang Keep, massacring Baron Silverlaine, Springvale, and the garrison.",al={"how did springvale die","who killed springvale","springvale death"}},{q="Why is Commander Springvale haunting Shadowfang Keep?",a="Twisted in death, his spirit remains bound by his final oaths. Springvale's ghost wanders the halls to defend the ruins and seek vengeance for his fallen lord against all who enter.",al={"why is springvale a ghost","springvale motive","why does springvale fight"}},{q="Why does a former paladin use unholy powers?",a="The violent trauma of his death and the dark magic pervading the keep corrupted his spirit. In his spectral state, the holy vows he once wielded have warped into vengeful, unholy power.",al={"why unholy magic","springvale unholy abilities","corrupted paladin"}},{q="Who was his master?",a="Commander Springvale served Baron Silverlaine, the noble ruler and master of Shadowfang Keep before Arugal's beasts devastated the estate.",al={"springvale master","who did springvale serve","springvale and silverlaine"}},{q="Where in the keep can he be found?",a="Commander Springvale's ghost is encountered deep within the keep, haunting the fortified chambers near the castle chapel and council rooms.",al={"springvale location","where is springvale","shadowfang springvale room"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="Springvale is a sobering reminder of how duty and sacred vows can curdle into eternal torment when an honorable knight is bound to a corrupted grave.",["faction:Alliance"]="Springvale represents the lost soldiers of Lordaeron and Gilneas, loyal defenders who fell not to the Scourge directly, but to the reckless summonings meant to stop them.",["faction:Horde"]="For the Forsaken reclaiming Silverpine Forest, laying the commander's shade to rest is another step in purging the remnants of Arugal's tragic failure."},kw={"arugal","commander","ghost","paladin","shadowfang","silverlaine","silverpine","springvale","worgen"},rel={"zone:shadowfang","npc:baron-silverlaine","npc:arugal","topic:worgen","topic:light","topic:scourge","topic:alliance","topic:horde"},src={"Commander Springvale"}}
E["npc:deathstalker-vincent"] = {t="npc",n="Deathstalker Vincent",z="shadowfang",s="Deathstalker Vincent was a Forsaken scout sent alongside Deathstalker Adamant to infiltrate Shadowfang Keep. Slain by the mad mage Arugal, his corpse remains inside the stronghold as a grim warning to any who challenge the feral worgen within.",h="Deathstalker Vincent was a Forsaken scout sent alongside Deathstalker Adamant to infiltrate Shadowfang Keep.",sec={{t="A Scout's Fatal End",b="Before the Forsaken could launch a full-scale assault against the beasts holding Shadowfang Keep, intelligence on the fortress's interior was desperately needed. Two operatives from the Deathstalkers, the intelligence arm of the Forsaken, slipped past the barricades: Vincent and Adamant. Their mission ended in disaster. While Adamant was captured and locked away in a dungeon cell, Vincent was dragged directly before Shadowfang's master. Refusing to bend the knee or serve Arugal's dark designs, Vincent was executed on the spot, his body discarded on the stone floor to rot as a testament to the mage's fury.",sp=0},{t="Arugal's Defiance",b="Arugal used Vincent's demise to issue a scathing declaration to the intruders in his keep. Confronting the captive operative, the mad mage mocked the Forsaken and compared their intrusion to the failed efforts of his former Kirin Tor comrades. Demanding that Vincent surrender his blade and secrets to his master, Arugal struck the scout down when he refused, declaring that Vincent's moldering remains would serve as a warning to anyone foolish enough to trespass in his domain.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Deathstalker Vincent?",a="Vincent was a Forsaken scout belonging to the Deathstalkers. He was dispatched with Deathstalker Adamant to gather critical reconnaissance inside Shadowfang Keep ahead of a planned assault by the Undercity.",al={"who is vincent","vincent shadowfang keep","dead rogue shadowfang"}},{q="What happened to Vincent in Shadowfang Keep?",a="Vincent was captured during his reconnaissance mission and executed by Archmage Arugal after refusing to defect or offer intelligence against the Forsaken. Arugal left his corpse where it fell as a display of power.",al={"how did vincent die","why is vincent dead","who killed vincent"}},{q="Where is his partner, Deathstalker Adamant?",a="While Vincent was executed out in the open, Deathstalker Adamant was captured alive and locked in a nearby dungeon cell under the watchful eye of a worgen guard.",al={"where is adamant","other deathstalker","adamant location"}},{q="Why were the Deathstalkers sent to Shadowfang Keep?",a="Silverpine Forest is vital territory for Sylvanas and the Forsaken, but Arugal's worgen hold the regional fortress of Shadowfang Keep. Vincent and Adamant were sent to scout the layout and defenses so the Forsaken could mount an effective offensive.",al={"why are deathstalkers in shadowfang","forsaken mission shadowfang"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Finding Vincent confirms the worst fears of the Forsaken commanders in Silverpine: the reconnaissance team failed, and the keep must now be cleared by force.",["class:Rogue"]="Vincent's execution stands as a sobering reminder of the risks faced by stealth operatives infiltrating hostile strongholds alone."},kw={"arugal","deathstalker adamant","deathstalker vincent","shadowfang keep","silverpine forest","vincent","worgen"},rel={"quest:1098","zone:shadowfang","npc:arugal","topic:forsaken","topic:worgen","topic:horde"},src={"Deathstalker Vincent"}}
E["npc:fenrus-the-devourer"] = {t="npc",n="Fenrus the Devourer",z="shadowfang",s="Fenrus the Devourer is an enormous worg that prowls the upper sanctum of Shadowfang Keep. Kept as a personal pet and guardian by Archmage Arugal, the ravenous beast is bloated on unnatural magics. Anyone daring to breach the archmage's personal study must contend with this feral horror and the master who watches over it.",h="Fenrus the Devourer is an enormous worg that prowls the upper sanctum of Shadowfang Keep.",sec={{t="A Beast in the Master's Study",b="Deep within Shadowfang Keep, just outside Archmage Arugal's personal chambers, lurks the monstrous worg known as Fenrus the Devourer. Unlike the lupine worgen roaming the ramparts, Fenrus is an actual worg, swollen to gargantuan proportions. Prowling the shelves, scrolls, and arcane apparatuses of Arugal's private study, the beast serves both as a pet and as a violent perimeter guard against any intruder seeking the mad mage's head.",sp=0},{t="Corrupted Might",b="Fenrus's unnatural bulk suggests he was subjected to the dark magics saturating the keep since Baron Silverlaine's downfall. Archmage Arugal or his unleashed worgen clearly warped the creature with arcane or shadowy experiments, transforming a native predator into a ravenous juggernaut. Fenrus is so feral and magically bound that no hunter can charm or tame his mind.",sp=0},{t="Arugal's Watchful Eye",b="Disturbing Fenrus is an immediate death sentence for the careless. When the beast spots an intruder, it lets loose an ear-splitting howl that echoes across the entire fortress, drawing the direct attention of Arugal himself. Rather than leaving his pet undefended, the archmage projects his dark will into the chamber, summoning voidwalkers to assist Fenrus in overwhelming and devouring invaders.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What kind of creature is Fenrus?",a="Fenrus is an exceptionally large worg, a natural wolf-like predator indigenous to Lordaeron, rather than a bipedal worgen. His unnatural bulk and vicious ferocity are the direct results of prolonged exposure to the dark magic practicing within Shadowfang Keep.",al={"is fenrus a worgen","fenrus creature type","fenrus wolf"}},{q="Where can Fenrus be found?",a="Fenrus prowls the study chambers high inside Shadowfang Keep in Silverpine Forest. His lair is situated directly along the approach to Archmage Arugal's inner redoubt.",al={"where is fenrus","fenrus location","fenrus room"}},{q="Can hunters tame Fenrus as a pet?",a="No. Despite being an ordinary beast by classification, Fenrus cannot be tamed. His mind is thoroughly broken, feral, and tied to Archmage Arugal's dark will.",al={"can i tame fenrus","is fenrus tameable","taming fenrus"}},{q="Why does Arugal summon demons when Fenrus is attacked?",a="Arugal views Fenrus as his prized pet and final line of defense before his sanctum. When Fenrus bellows upon entering combat, Arugal intervenes directly, conjuring voidwalkers into the chamber to overwhelm whoever threatens his beast.",al={"arugal voidwalkers","why does arugal help fenrus","fenrus voidwalker add"}},{q="Why is Fenrus so much larger than normal worgs?",a="Fenrus's massive size is believed to be the consequence of Archmage Arugal's dark magical experimentation, or magical fallout from the worgen infestation overtaking the keep.",al={"why is fenrus huge","fenrus size lore","giant worg"}},{q="What happens across the dungeon when Fenrus is engaged?",a="When Fenrus engages in combat, he unleashes a thunderous roar so loud it can be heard by anyone anywhere inside Shadowfang Keep, alerting all to the battle taking place outside Arugal's door.",al={"fenrus roar","fenrus howl across dungeon","loud roar sfk"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="Do not waste time attempting to charm Fenrus. The beast's mind is irrevocably twisted by Shadowfang's dark arts and cannot be bound by the wild.",["class:Warlock"]="Archmage Arugal's ability to summon voidwalkers to aid his hound reveals how deeply the former Dalaran mage has delved into shadowy, forbidden conjurations.",["class:Mage"]="Fenrus stands as a grim reminder of how far Archmage Arugal has fallen, using arcane arts to warp wild beasts into grotesque domestic guardians."},kw={"arugal","fenrus","fenrus the devourer","shadowfang keep","silverpine","worg"},rel={"npc:arugal","zone:shadowfang","topic:worgen"},src={"Fenrus the Devourer"}}
E["npc:keeper-bel-dugur"] = {t="npc",n="Keeper Bel'dugur",z="shadowfang",s="Keeper Bel'dugur is a scholarly Forsaken residing deep within the Apothecarium of the Undercity. He serves his people by commissioning expeditions to recover dark tomes and magical artifacts from across Azeroth.",h="Keeper Bel'dugur is a scholarly Forsaken residing deep within the Apothecarium of the Undercity.",sec={{t="A Collector of Dark Relics",b="Situated among the vats and researchers of the Apothecarium, Keeper Bel'dugur tasks adventurers with retrieving dangerous arcane and occult relics from across Azeroth. Among his most prominent interests is the Book of Ur, a legendary treatise on extra-dimensional beings locked away inside Shadowfang Keep. While many in the Undercity seek magical knowledge to cure or weaponize the condition of the undead, Bel'dugur's curated acquisitions appear tailored toward unearthing ancient, forbidden powers.",sp=0},{t="Hidden Loyalties",b="Beneath his calm demeanor as an Undercity researcher lies a covert loyalty to the apocalyptic Twilight's Hammer cult. The quests and research tasks Bel'dugur assigns quietly further the cult's esoteric agenda, acquiring foundational grimoires of summoning and void magic under the unsuspecting nose of the Royal Apothecary Society and Lady Sylvanas.",sp=2}},faq={{q="Where can I find Keeper Bel'dugur?",a="Keeper Bel'dugur is located in the Apothecarium, the alchemical district nestled within the southern lower ring of the Undercity.",al={"keeper bel'dugur location","where is beldugur","beldugur map"}},{q="Why does Bel'dugur want The Book of Ur?",a="The Book of Ur contains the foundational research of the Dalaran mage Ur regarding other dimensions and the feral worgen. Bel'dugur seeks to harness these forbidden summoning principles for the dark schemes of his true masters.",al={"why book of ur","what does beldugur do with book of ur"},sp=1},{q="Is Keeper Bel'dugur loyal to Lady Sylvanas?",a="Outwardly, he functions as an archivist and researcher for the Forsaken. In truth, subtle hints in his investigations reveal he operates as an undercover agent for the sinister Twilight's Hammer cult.",al={"is beldugur evil","beldugur faction","who does beldugur serve"},sp=2},{q="What other tasks does he give adventurers?",a="Beyond Shadowfang Keep's Book of Ur, Bel'dugur directs travelers toward forgotten lore and forbidden tomes, including dark treatises tied to ancient rituals and forbidden knowledge.",al={"beldugur quests","keeper beldugur quests"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Bel'dugur seems like any other scholarly Forsaken seeking forbidden knowledge to bolster your kingdom, but his true ambitions lie outside the Banshee Queen's survivalist cause.",["class:Warlock"]="Warlocks frequently cross paths with Bel'dugur's requests, as his interests align heavily with dangerous grimoires, extraplanar summoning, and dark occultism."},kw={"apothecarium","bel'dugur","keeper beldugur","shadowfang","the book of ur","undercity"},rel={"subzone:apothecarium","zone:undercity","quest:1013","topic:twilight-s-hammer","zone:shadowfang","topic:forsaken"},src={"Keeper Bel'dugur"}}
E["quest:1013"] = {t="quest",n="The Book of Ur",z="shadowfang",s="The Book of Ur is a mission assigned by Keeper Bel'dugur in the Undercity's Apothecarium. Bel'dugur charges Horde champions with infiltrating Shadowfang Keep to recover the arcane treatise of Ur, a deceased mage of Dalaran. The Forsaken seek Ur's extraplanar research, intending to weaponize magical insights he was too scrupulous to exploit.",h="The Book of Ur is a mission assigned by Keeper Bel'dugur in the Undercity's Apothecarium.",sec={{t="A Relic of Extramundane Magic",b="Before the Third War wiped out Dalaran, a brilliant human wizard named Ur dedicated his scholarship to realms beyond Azeroth. Unlike standard Kirin Tor doctrine, which strictly regulated conjuration and outer planar contacts, Ur cataloged entities from other dimensions, including the savage worgen. Despite his curiosity, Ur ultimately hesitated to manipulate these alien powers, deeming them dangerously uncontrollable. That restraint, however, made his written legacy a coveted prize for those who possess no such moral qualms.",sp=0},{t="The Fall into Dark Hands",b="Following Ur's demise during the Scourge invasion of Dalaran, his works scattered. His definitive treatise found its way into the clutches of Archmage Arugal, a grieving and unstable wizard who holed up in Shadowfang Keep. Arugal lacked Ur's ethical reservations and used the book's contents to summon bloodthirsty worgen into Silverpine, unleashing a curse that devoured Pyrewood and the surrounding valleys. The volume now rests neglected inside the keep's towers, watched over by Arugal's feral pets.",sp=0},{t="The Forsaken's Ambition",b="To the Royal Apothecary Society and Keeper Bel'dugur, Ur's downfall was not a cautionary tale of hubris, but an example of mortal frailty. Bel'dugur believes Ur perished because conscience paralyzed him at the moment of crisis. By securing the Book of Ur for the Undercity, the Forsaken intend to strip the text of its academic hesitation, harnessing extradimensional lore to ensure their survival and enforce Sylvanas Windrunner's dominion across Lordaeron.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Ur?",a="Ur was a notable Dalaran mage who studied magical phenomena and other worlds prior to the Third War. He extensively researched extradimensional creatures, including the worgen, before being killed during the Scourge invasion of Dalaran.",al={"ur lore","who is ur","mage ur"}},{q="Where is the Book of Ur located?",a="The book rests inside Shadowfang Keep, resting on a bookshelf within the chamber belonging to Fenrus the Devourer, deep within the fortress.",al={"where is the book","book of ur location","shadowfang book location"}},{q="Who is Keeper Bel'dugur?",a="Keeper Bel'dugur is a Forsaken archivist and researcher stationed in the Apothecarium of the Undercity. He gathers dark, arcane, and extramundane lore to advance the power and survival of the Forsaken.",al={"beldugur","keeper bel dugur","quest giver"}},{q="Why does the Forsaken want the book?",a="Bel'dugur and his cohort desire Ur's research into extraplanar entities. The Forsaken believe Ur failed to survive the Scourge only because his moral conscience held him back from exploiting the powers he discovered—a hesitation the Undercity has no intention of repeating.",al={"why do forsaken want ur's book","undercity purpose book of ur"}},{q="How did the book end up in Shadowfang Keep?",a="After Dalaran's fall, Archmage Arugal acquired Ur's notes and utilized them to summon the worgen into Lordaeron. Arugal brought the research to Shadowfang Keep when he seized the fortress.",al={"how did arugal get the book","why is the book in sfk"}},{q="Is the Book of Ur related to the worgen curse?",a="Yes. Ur's research detailed the terrifying dimension from which worgen originate. Arugal used the treatise to unleash those beasts upon Silverpine Forest, resulting in the infestation plaguing the region.",al={"worgen origin book","book of ur worgen"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="The Book of Ur serves as a grim artifact of Kirin Tor history, showing how Dalaran's theoretical research into otherworldly entities could be twisted into apocalyptic curses by unstable practitioners like Arugal.",["class:Warlock"]="Ur's willingness to peer beyond mortal reality mirrors a warlock's hunger for extraplanar knowledge, though Bel'dugur notes that Ur's failure lay in lacking the nerve to wield what he discovered.",["race:Undead"]="Retrieving the book directly serves Lady Sylvanas and the Royal Apothecary Society, reinforcing the Forsaken belief that survival requires embracing forbidden lore without mortal squeamishness.",["faction:Horde"]="Clearing Shadowfang Keep and securing Arugal's sources helps stabilize Silverpine Forest, curbing the feral worgen menace encroaching on Horde-held territories."},kw={"apothecarium","arugal","bel'dugur","book of ur","dalaran","fenrus","kirin tor","shadowfang keep","worgen"},rel={"npc:keeper-bel-dugur","zone:shadowfang","subzone:apothecarium","zone:undercity","subzone:dalaran","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge"},m={start="Keeper Bel'dugur",level="26",faction="Horde",id=1013},src={"The Book of Ur (quest)"}}
E["quest:1014"] = {t="quest",n="Arugal Must Die",z="shadowfang",s="Arugal Must Die is a decisive Horde mission issued by Dalar Dawnweaver at the Sepulcher. It tasks brave champions with storming Shadowfang Keep to slay the rogue archmage Archmage Arugal and claim his severed head. Eliminating Arugal is critical for Lady Sylvanas Windrunner to break the worgen menace and secure Silverpine Forest for the Forsaken.",h="Arugal Must Die is a decisive Horde mission issued by Dalar Dawnweaver at the Sepulcher.",sec={{t="A Thorn in the Dark Lady's Side",b="While the Forsaken have carved out a base in the Sepulcher, Silverpine Forest remains treacherous and deeply contested. Perched high upon the cliffs overlooking the woods sits Shadowfang Keep, the lair of Archmage Arugal. Driven mad by guilt and dark sorcery, Arugal unleashed the feral worgen upon Lordaeron. His ravenous beasts roam the forest paths, directly hindering Lady Sylvanas Windrunner's efforts to establish a fortified strategic hold over the region.",sp=0},{t="Striking the Beast at the Neck",b="Dalar Dawnweaver recognizes that merely hunting wandering beasts in the forest will never cleanse the land. The heart of the corruption beats within Shadowfang Keep itself. Horde champions must breach the ancient stronghold, fight through Arugal's devoted worgen brood, and confront the mad wizard in his aerie. Bringing his head back to the Sepulcher finally shatters his magical hold over the region, clearing the way for Forsaken supremacy.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Dalar Dawnweaver want Arugal dead?",a="Dalar Dawnweaver acts under the orders of the Dark Lady. Arugal's worgen overrun Silverpine Forest, making it impossible for the Forsaken to turn the region into a secure strategic stronghold until the mad mage is slain.",al={"why kill arugal","dalar dawnweaver goal","arugal target"}},{q="Where can Arugal be found?",a="Archmage Arugal resides at the very peak of Shadowfang Keep, a grim fortress looming over southern Silverpine Forest.",al={"where is arugal","arugal location","find arugal"}},{q="What proof is required to complete the mission?",a="Dalar Dawnweaver requires tangible proof of the wizard's demise: champions must retrieve and present the severed Head of Arugal.",al={"what does dalar need","arugal head quest","proof of death"}},{q="What threat does Arugal pose to the Horde?",a="Beyond his potent offensive magics, Arugal commands legions of cursed worgen that harass Horde forces and threaten Forsaken control throughout Silverpine Forest.",al={"why is arugal dangerous","worgen threat silverpine","is arugal a threat"}},{q="Who does Dalar Dawnweaver serve?",a="Dalar Dawnweaver serves Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the Forsaken, operating out of the Sepulcher to consolidate Forsaken control across Lordaeron.",al={"who does dawnweaver work for","sepulcher leadership"}},{q="What happens after Arugal is defeated?",a="With Arugal's death, his foul magical grip over Silverpine is broken, allowing the Forsaken to expand their dominance across western Lordaeron without fear of his coordinated worgen packs.",al={"after arugal dies","result of arugal death"},sp=1}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, eliminating Arugal secures their southwestern border and ensures the safety of routes connecting the Sepulcher to the Undercity.",["faction:Horde"]="Taking down Arugal demonstrates the Horde's growing martial reach in the Eastern Kingdoms, breaking an entrenched wizard and freeing vital roads.",["class:Mage"]="Confronting Arugal serves as a cautionary tale of arcane hubris, pitting practitioners of the magical arts against a Kirin Tor mage warped by otherworldly summons."},kw={"arugal","dalar dawnweaver","head of arugal","sepulcher","shadowfang keep","silverpine","sylvanas","worgen"},rel={"npc:arugal","npc:dalar-dawnweaver","zone:shadowfang","zone:silverpine","subzone:sepulcher","topic:lordaeron"},m={start="Dalar Dawnweaver",level="27",faction="Horde",id=1014},src={"Arugal Must Die"}}
E["quest:1098"] = {t="quest",n="Deathstalkers in Shadowfang",z="shadowfang",s="High Executor Hadrec dispatches Horde adventurers into Shadowfang Keep to locate two missing reconnaissance agents, Deathstalker Adamant and Deathstalker Vincent. The Forsaken military relies on their gathered intelligence to coordinate an assault against Archmage Arugal and his worgen packs. Breaching the fortress reveals the grim reality of espionage behind enemy lines.",h="High Executor Hadrec dispatches Horde adventurers into Shadowfang Keep to locate two missing reconnaissance...",sec={{t="Into the Worgen Den",b="Silverpine Forest remains contested ground, with Archmage Arugal's feral worgen holding the towering redoubt of Shadowfang Keep. Seeking to break this siege on their southern borders, the Forsaken command stationed at the Sepulcher organized an intelligence operation. High Executor Hadrec sent two seasoned Deathstalkers—Adamant and Vincent—to infiltrate the fortress and chart its defenses. When days passed without word, Hadrec grew desperate for their field reports, tasking capable Horde champions with entering the stronghold to recover the agents and salvage the mission.",sp=0},{t="A Bitter Discovery",b="Upon fighting their way through the lower ramparts, adventurers discover the heavy price of the infiltration. While Deathstalker Adamant survives in captivity and assists in unbarring the courtyard gates, Vincent met a brutal end. His broken corpse lies motionless within the keep, his personal intelligence lost to the dark halls. Only a small trinket remains clenched in his cold fingers, serving as quiet testament to a spy who gave his unlife for the Dark Lady's conquest.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why were Deathstalkers sent to Shadowfang Keep?",a="High Executor Hadrec ordered the infiltration to gather vital tactical intelligence on Archmage Arugal's forces and fortifications before committing Forsaken troops to a full-scale assault on Shadowfang Keep.",al={"why send spies to shadowfang","hadrec mission purpose","deathstalker goal shadowfang"}},{q="Who are Deathstalkers Adamant and Vincent?",a="They are elite Forsaken operatives belonging to the Deathstalkers, the espionage and assassination branch of the Undercity. Sent ahead as advance scouts, they were tasked with mapping Shadowfang Keep and observing the worgen defenses.",al={"who are adamant and vincent","adamant and vincent lore"}},{q="What happened to Deathstalker Vincent?",a="Vincent was killed by the denizens of the keep during the mission. Adventurers find his broken body lying just beyond the courtyard gate, clutching a small trinket in his hand.",al={"did vincent die","where is vincent","vincent fate"},sp=1},{q="What role does Deathstalker Adamant play inside the keep?",a="Adamant survives the initial infiltration, though he is trapped. When adventurers reach him, he helps unlock the courtyard gate, allowing the assault deeper into the fortress to proceed while he relays what intelligence he can back to Hadrec.",al={"what does adamant do","deathstalker adamant role"},sp=1},{q="Where does this mission begin?",a="The mission is given by High Executor Hadrec, the Forsaken military commander stationed at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest.",al={"where to get deathstalkers in shadowfang","quest giver deathstalkers in shadowfang"}},{q="Why does the Forsaken leadership want Shadowfang Keep cleared?",a="Archmage Arugal unleashes violent worgen packs across Silverpine Forest from his perch in Shadowfang Keep, constantly threatening Forsaken holdings, supply lines, and the overall security of Lordaeron.",al={"why attack shadowfang","forsaken beef with arugal"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, reclaiming Silverpine from Arugal's beasts is essential to securing the borders of Lordaeron, making Vincent's sacrifice a somber reminder of the cost of their freedom.",["class:Rogue"]="The fallen Vincent and the captured Adamant demonstrate the lethal risks of deep reconnaissance work behind heavily fortified enemy lines.",["faction:Horde"]="High Executor Hadrec relies on Horde champions to support Forsaken operations when conventional troops cannot breach Arugal's cursed fortress."},kw={"adamant","arugal","deathstalkers in shadowfang","hadrec","sepulcher","shadowfang keep","silverpine","vincent"},rel={"npc:high-executor-hadrec","npc:deathstalker-vincent","zone:shadowfang","quest:1886","quest:448"},m={start="High Executor Hadrec",["end"]="Deathstalker Vincent",level="25",faction="Horde",id=1098},src={"Deathstalkers in Shadowfang"}}
E["zone:shadowfang"] = {t="dungeon",n="Shadowfang Keep",z="shadowfang",s="Perched on the rugged bluffs above Pyrewood Village, Shadowfang Keep is the gloomy stronghold of the rogue Kirin Tor wizard, Archmage Arugal. Once the ancestral estate of Baron Silverlaine, the bastion now teems with feral worgen beasts and the tormented phantoms of its slaughtered defenders. For adventurers traversing southern Silverpine, the keep represents the dark epicenter of the beastly scourge consuming the region.",h="Perched on the rugged bluffs above Pyrewood Village, Shadowfang Keep is the gloomy stronghold of the rogue...",sec={{t="Fall of the Silverlaine Dynasty",b="Before it was shrouded in nightmare, Shadowfang was known as Silverlaine Keep, a noble seat loyal to Gilnean lords and garrisoned by the pious Commander Springvale. When the Scourge swept through Lordaeron during the Third War, Dalaran's wizards fell in droves. Desperate to stem the rising dead, Archmage Arugal defied Kirin Tor leadership and delved into the research of the wizard Ur, summoning extra-dimensional worgen to turn the tide. The summoned beasts savaged the undead, but rapidly slipped beyond all mortal control, breaking into southern Silverpine and storming the bastion. Baron Silverlaine and his entire court were massacred, doomed to haunt the stone halls alongside the feral monsters that overran their home.",sp=0},{t="Arugal's Children",b="Broken by guilt and madness, Arugal retreated within the blood-stained battlements, adopting the ravenous wolf-men as his beloved 'children' and christening the castle Shadowfang Keep. Deep in the stone roosts, lupine packs and shadowy hounds flourish under trainers like Wolf Master Nandos, watched over by Arugal's massive lupine beast, Fenrus the Devourer. Outside the walls, the curse did not halt; nearby Pyrewood Village remains trapped in a horrifying nocturnal cycle, its residents walking as men by day and hunting as ravenous worgen beneath the moon, tethered inexorably to the mad archmage perched on the heights above.",sp=0},{t="The Forsaken Strike",b="Recognizing the dire threat Arugal poses to their dominion in Silverpine Forest, Lady Sylvanas Windrunner dispatched the Royal Apothecary Society and elite Deathstalkers to root out the source of the worgen curse. Infiltration teams suffered brutal casualties within the dungeons, but Horde heroes answering the call from the Sepulcher ultimately breach the highest tower. Striking down the Archmage brings a formal end to the master of the pack, severing the mind orchestrating the beasts' spread across the wilderness and claiming his head as proof of Lordaeron's vengeance.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What happens when Archmage Arugal is defeated?",a="Slaying Arugal decapitates the central force controlling the worgen packs in southern Silverpine. Horde adventurers deliver his severed head to Deathstalker Vincent at the Sepulcher under orders from Lady Sylvanas Windrunner. While his demise breaks the direct will directing the Shadowfang pack, the feral beasts and ghostly remnants lingering in the keep and the surrounding woods remain a persistent danger to travelers.",al={"kill arugal outcome","arugal dead lore","what happens after arugal dies"},sp=1},{q="Why did Arugal summon the worgen?",a="During the Third War, the armies of Dalaran were suffering disastrous defeats against the Scourge. Fallen wizards continuously rose as undead soldiers for the Lich King. Seeking a weapon to turn the tide, Arugal used the arcane research of the wizard Ur to summon extra-dimensional worgen, believing their savagery could halt the Scourge.",al={"why worgen summoned","arugal motive","dalaran worgen summon"}},{q="Who was Baron Silverlaine?",a="Baron Silverlaine was the human nobleman who ruled the keep and oversaw the neighboring hamlet of Pyrewood before the Third War. When Arugal's summoned beasts escaped control, they stormed the stronghold and butchered the baron, his household, and his guards. Silverlaine's vengeful ghost still haunts the great dining halls, cursed to walk alongside the monsters that slew him.",al={"baron silverlaine lore","original lord of shadowfang"}},{q="Why are Pyrewood Village villagers friendly during the day?",a="Arugal subjected the inhabitants of nearby Pyrewood Village to his dark magic. By day, they retain their human form, minds, and peaceful demeanor toward Alliance travelers. At sundown, the curse takes hold, transforming the entire population into savage worgen loyal to the mad archmage in the keep.",al={"pyrewood humans","pyrewood curse","why pyrewood turns worgen"}},{q="Who is Commander Springvale?",a="Commander Springvale was a paladin of the Silver Hand and the military officer responsible for defending Silverlaine Keep. When the worgen overrun the stronghold, he fought to the death. His restless spirit still patrols the upper hallways, clinging to martial duty even in undeath.",al={"springvale lore","ghostly paladin boss"}},{q="What is the Book of Ur?",a="The Book of Ur is a tome containing the research of Ur, an archmage of Dalaran who studied extra-dimensional entities, including the worgen. Arugal used Ur's writings to perform his disastrous summons. The Royal Apothecary Society in the Undercity seeks the book to understand the nature of the wolf-creatures and their bizarre magic.",al={"book of ur quest","ur lore"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The Forsaken view Arugal's encroaching packs as an immediate danger to their fledgling territory in Silverpine, making the keep a priority target for Deathstalker operatives and the Royal Apothecary Society.",["class:Mage"]="The tragedy of Shadowfang serves as a grim warning of what happens when a Kirin Tor wizard meddles in extra-dimensional summoning beyond mortal control.",["class:Warlock"]="The dark energies, voidwalkers, and fell sorceries inside the keep draw the interest of practitioners looking to recover ancient relics like the Orb of Soran'ruk.",["class:Paladin"]="The restless spirit of Commander Springvale stands as a sorrowful reminder of fallen Silver Hand defenders whose sacred oaths were warped by death."},kw={"arugal","fenrus","pyrewood","sfk","shadowfang","silverlaine","silverpine","springvale","worgen"},rel={"npc:arugal","npc:baron-silverlaine","npc:commander-springvale","quest:1014","quest:1013","subzone:pyrewood-village","zone:silverpine","topic:worgen"},m={levels="22-30"},src={"Shadowfang Keep (Classic)","Shadowfang Keep"}}
